Rewrite the requirements listed as failing in the QA feedback below. Apply the specific changes requested for each requirement ID. Leave all other requirements exactly as they are. Output the complete requirements document (all requirements, revised and unchanged) in the same format as the original.

IMPORTANT: For any QA issue that cannot be resolved from the transcript alone (e.g., phone/email verification methods, documentation matrix, address-processing rules, status finalization), explicitly mark that requirement as PENDING STAKEHOLDER INPUT and state what decision is needed — do not leave the issue unresolved without explanation.

ORIGINAL REQUIREMENTS DOCUMENT:
{requirements}

QA FEEDBACK:
{qa_feedback}

Compare the revised requirements document (produced by the previous task) against the QA feedback below. For each issue the QA reviewer raised, confirm whether it has been resolved in the revision or marked PENDING STAKEHOLDER INPUT with a clear explanation. Produce a short checklist: [RESOLVED], [PENDING STAKEHOLDER INPUT], or [STILL OPEN] for each QA issue, and output the final revised requirements document in full.

QA FEEDBACK TO CHECK AGAINST:
{qa_feedback}
